go to matt finn who's on the ground  outside in minneapolis matt  hey guys this is becoming an escalating  scene here outside of the rally a short  while ago we saw people lighting  maga hats on fire lighting other things  on fire people  rushing police throwing objects at  police calling them pigs  and happening here right now there's a  confrontation of  reporters lined up against police it's  kind of settled down now but  uh for a while there this was a pretty  intense scene  here comes something that was just  thrown out i don't know a cup or  something at police officers but  you know the scene all night long has  been intensifying people  have been in our faces there have been  instigators there have been a few  characters  who sought to uh to disrupt and suppress  media crews here tonight  and uh it seems like right now this is  uh coming to a point where hopefully  things will  eventually settle we'll continue to  monitor this and update you throughout  the night  but matt matt i got a question for you  if you can hear me what's going to  happen when you got 20  000 trump supporters exit those  buildings  wearing those maga hats  what is that question what is going to  happen when the  20 000 people that are trump supporters  exit that building that's what we've  kind of been bracing for  i guess it's anyone's guess there are  police here in riot gear  there are police close nearby around the  block there is certainly a very large  police presence we see buses  we see all types of vehicles and there  i've  i mean you might be able to see some on  camera but there are some bad actors in  this crowd tonight we have experienced  them  they have been vulgar they have been  jumping in front of our cameras cursing  at us  which is typical for any protest i have  personally covered  crowds and protests outside of donald  trump rallies across this country  and tonight i would say is right up  there with a crowd that has some of the  worst instigators and  uh you know we witnessed some type of  what might have been tear gas  earlier there's something else that was  just thrown at a police officer on a  horse  these people are calling officers pigs  so unfortunately there are some people  here some protesters  who are exercising their freedom of  speech and right to protest but also  instigating matt how many people are we  talking about in this uh  this riotous type of atmosphere that  you're in how many people are protesting  i hate to use numbers on air because  then we get criticized for  you know giving the wrong estimate but i  would say you know we see at least  hundreds of people here right now and  early in the night there were  at least 1 000 protesters here and that  might be a low estimate  so again as people are now the rally is  wrapped up do you see  any of those people in the arena  actually coming out and getting close to  what we're seeing on camera  so what you're seeing on camera is uh  this line between police and  demonstrators and  because the protesters kind of rushed  police they actually rushed in the  opposite direction of the arena these  these protesters now are facing away  from the arena so  uh i can't tell from my vantage point  but perhaps the the president trump  supporters are  exiting the arena without running into  these people  right now and when they started to come  into the arena were the protesters  though allowed to get in close proximity  to those people  or were they separated into a different  area  uh so we've been out here all day and  you know as we see with trump rallies  across the country  thousands and uh there's another object  just throwing it the horse  uh you know the horse are obviously  reacting to this but  to answer your question uh you know  we're out here all day thousands and  thousands of people lined up  but they uh they were separated from the  protesters and the majority of the  protesters you're seeing here right now  did not arrive until later in the  evening so the majority of the president  trump supporters lining up to get inside  of the rally  did not face these protesters on the way  in but it seems like there are certainly  going to be some that are going to have  to face them  on the way out we see a number of people  with signs and when they're yelling and  screaming things can you give us a sense  of  what is their message  we're hearing some of the signature  chants who streets our streets  shut it down um you know i can't confirm  but our crew and our security identified  what are probably members of antifa  uh they have met you know they have the  handkerchiefs covering their mouths we  had to relocate several times throughout  the night  uh we're we are okay but there were  several times when instigators were  going to clearly interfere  with our reports and that's what they  wanted to do and and that's their  message that they come here to shut it  down and  that's what they're doing we saw one  maybe two fires just  moments ago what very much appeared to  be maga hats on fire we saw people  cursing police  rushing at them throwing all types of  objects at them and we're still  witnessing that right now people are  throwing bottles at police on horses  the horses are reacting they're backing  up there were a couple moments just a  short while ago that were very intense  this now is  a much more calm scene but there are  still a lot of people out here  and there are still a lot of police  pushing back matt thank you for that  report  and stay safe
 

